"""rlinux-port: do the mechanical part of porting a small C driver to Rust.

  rlinux-port analyze  <driver.c | REV:path>   facts + Rust-abstraction verdict
  rlinux-port scaffold <driver.c> [--keep-c]   generate <driver>.rs, Kconfig/CI edits
  rlinux-port compare  <REV:driver.c> <driver.rs>
                                               register accesses C vs Rust,
                                               leftover TODO(port) markers
  rlinux-port api-index [--out FILE]           one-line index of rust/kernel APIs

Run from the top of an rlinux tree. Function bodies are never translated:
`scaffold` pastes each C body into the Rust stub as a comment and leaves a
`TODO(port)` marker; translating it is the porter's job. See README.md.
"""

